s $36$ feet. Now, to find the unit price per foot, we divide the total price by $36:$  \n\n$$\n19.80÷36=0.55\n$$\n\nTherefore, the copper wire costs $$0.55$ per foot."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495080 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495044 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "247d98e4-8f13-5536-8ad6-00a14e476caf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Unit Price With Conversion to Larger Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07912185-c7d5-5b6c-8f45-d654e8135980" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$4.20$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494334} {:answer/id #uuid "61c41dea-cdf7-5e2d-afde-16a710ed4494" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$4.80$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494518} {:answer/id #uuid "9456679f-7480-577e-8233-cf7d29a74379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$3.60$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494658} {:answer/id #uuid "a1a51270-a0e0-5fd7-af26-acdedbf69bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$3.00$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494687} {:answer/id #uuid "cc1a86d7-b878-5ff2-8d27-3fe8e4fc81e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$2.40$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494799}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9456679f-7480-577e-8233-cf7d29a74379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$3.60$ per yard" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494658} :answer-field/id #uuid "98137096-8693-5fae-be94-43f600d56c9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494990}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "439aee16-5dee-54f4-90f1-94c1e1c52d92" :question/math-academy-id "q-354921" :question/problem "David bought $1$ foot of decorative ribbon and paid $$1.20$ for it. What's the unit price per yard?\n\nAssume that there are $3$ feet in one yard." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that there are $3$ feet in each yard.  \n\nSince the price is $$1.20$ per foot, to find the price per yard, we multiply by $3:$\n\n$$\n1.20\\times 3=3.60\n$$\n\nTherefore, the decorative ribbon costs $$3.60$ per yard."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495104 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495044 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "247d98e4-8f13-5536-8ad6-00a14e476caf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Unit Price With Conversion to Larger Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "081f659b-8624-5b9b-989e-42fbc2e410fa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$8.50$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494339} {:answer/id #uuid "23f69f50-a53b-5f9a-ac59-d504d7890862" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$8.85$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494387} {:answer/id #uuid "2ba9a5e4-76a7-501d-a2a3-d2bb93ec1427" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$0.57$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494402} {:answer/id #uuid "487fd89e-e1d0-52fb-8307-e15d8b284aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$9.12$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494466} {:answer/id #uuid "dd227569-9234-512c-9803-3479e03530a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$9.50$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "487fd89e-e1d0-52fb-8307-e15d8b284aa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$9.12$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494466} :answer-field/id #uuid "26bbc1b2-513a-5ed8-8d12-f14104359b36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "80687806-40a5-5de4-a9f6-85c3a9e00b61" :question/math-academy-id "q-354927" :question/problem "A chef bought $80$ ounces of spices and paid $$45.60$ for them. What's the unit price per pound?\n\nAssume that there are $16$ ounces in one pound." :question/worked-solution "First, we convert from ounces to pounds. There are $16$ ounces in each pound, so we divide the number of ounces by $16:$     \n\n$$\n80÷16=5\n$$\n\nSo, $80$ ounces is the same as $5$ pounds. Now, to find the unit price per pound, we divide the total price by $5:$ \n\n$$\n45.60÷5=9.12\n$$\n\nTherefore, the spices cost $$9.12$ per pound."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495127 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495044 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "247d98e4-8f13-5536-8ad6-00a14e476caf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Unit Price With Conversion to Larger Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "050fa726-2681-5eee-a791-6c3774b790f3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$16$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494328} {:answer/id #uuid "531a5fbe-a36d-5dbb-932a-1bb013b3395e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$24$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494485} {:answer/id #uuid "8e2b2b93-6dcd-535e-ba5a-8e58eb67c446" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$22$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494641} {:answer/id #uuid "8f36fd1f-8875-5422-aadc-3005fb55784a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$20$ per pound" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494643} {:answer/id #