t price per gallon, we divide the total price by $5:$ \n\n$$\n16.80÷5=3.36\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gasoline costs $$3.36$ per gallon."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495130 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495044 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "247d98e4-8f13-5536-8ad6-00a14e476caf" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Unit Price With Conversion to Larger Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1efe9830-e903-5ad3-a8c7-c7731a61db0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$1.80$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494377} {:answer/id #uuid "3fdc82a0-9a27-58fb-b6e8-c19566c4f986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$2.00$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494450} {:answer/id #uuid "822b6e3d-c5fe-5f8f-9d7a-2aa5d20d974d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$2.10$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494602} {:answer/id #uuid "d0f3ba0d-c418-5d69-88a6-cd1f93e16945" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$1.95$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494815} {:answer/id #uuid "db6aa90a-be97-5e18-a619-ce9042ab8c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$2.20$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494836}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3fdc82a0-9a27-58fb-b6e8-c19566c4f986" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$2.00$ per cup" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494450} :answer-field/id #uuid "c14baa77-de49-5b0a-b3aa-d1c3e71903fa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186495009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b7148b05-c37b-56db-9e21-9c51d5a86ad3" :question/math-academy-id "q-68547" :question/problem "A pack contains $24$ fluid ounce of cream cheese and costs $$6.00.$ What's the unit price per cup?\n\nAssume that there are $8$ fluid ounces in one cup." :question/worked-solution "First, we convert from fluid ounces to cups. There are $8$ fluid ounces in each cup, so we divide the number of fluid ounces by $8:$  \n\n$$\n24÷8=3\n$$\n\nSo, $24$ fluid ounces is the same as $3$ cups. Now, to find the unit price per cup, we divide the total price by $3:$ \n\n$$\n6.00÷3=2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the cream cheese costs $$2.00$ per cup."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495113 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186495045 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "60ccce15-6e30-58e5-a087-52100ebb460b" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Unit Price With Conversion to Smaller Units"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33773bf4-7ba5-53c7-a6f7-1db71c1ce387" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$239$ per foot" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494420} {:answer/id #uuid "83899377-100f-57b0-82bc-74722fe6ffc8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$241$ per foot" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494606} {:answer/id #uuid "98c55755-3c28-51fe-a698-ec2bf89cf7c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$235$ per foot" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494666} {:answer/id #uuid "9b741cdb-db66-5bd2-a07a-5720cb59717b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$237$ per foot" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494674} {:answer/id #uuid "f48f8c3c-3f9e-5c75-80b4-168bbfd56212" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$243$ per foot" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494900}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b741cdb-db66-5bd2-a07a-5720cb59717b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$$237$ per foot" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494674} :answer-field/id #uuid "48a2fc9a-c8e6-530f-93c5-a85ff3637db5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186494950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9154bcfc-535d-5b52-8c6a-5ddc0039e572" :question/math-academy-id "q-68573" :question/problem "Repaving a country road costs $$711$  per yard. What's the unit price per foot?\n\nAssume that there are $3$ feet in one yard." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that there are $3$ feet in $1$ yard. So, to find the unit price per foot, we divide the total price by $3:$\n\n$$\n711÷3=237\n$$\n\nTherefore, resurfacing the road costs $$237$ per foot."}]}
